The '''Alliance Remnants'''<ref name="Shards of the Alliance">[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Shards_of_the_Alliance_(WC3_NightElf) Shards of the Alliance (WC3 NightElf)]</ref><ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ruins_of_Dalaran_(WC3_NightElf) The Ruins of Dalaran (WC3 NightElf)]</ref><ref name="Misconceptions">[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Misconceptions_(WC3_BloodElf) Misconceptions (WC3 BloodElf)]</ref> (normally referred to as simply the '''Alliance'''<ref name="Dreadlord's Fall">[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Dreadlord%27s_Fall_(WC3_Undead) Dreadlord's Fall (WC3 Undead)]</ref><ref name="A New Power in Lordaeron">[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/A_New_Power_in_Lordaeron_(WC3_Undead) A New Power in Lordaeron (WC3 Undead)]</ref><ref>[[Captain Silas' Letter]]</ref> or the '''Remnants''',<ref name="ACtA1">{{questlong|Alliance|17|A Call to Aid}}</ref> also known as the '''Lordaeron Remnants''')<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20260514170802/https://turtlecraft.gg/new-locations-and-maps New Zones & World Edits]. Archived from [https://turtlecraft.gg/new-locations-and-maps the original] on 2026-05-14. Retrieved on 2026-29-08.</ref> are a force that has operated since the aftermath of the [[Third War]] and consisted of [[human]]s, [[Kirin Tor]], [[Blood elf|blood elves]] and [[Dwarf|dwarves]] (under both Bronzebeard<ref name="Misconceptions" /> and Wildhammer<ref name="Dreadlord's Fall" />) formerly led by Grand Marshal [[Othmar Garithos]] and Prince [[Kael'thas Sunstrider]].

Following the death of Grand Marshal Garithos, the Remnants remain an [[Alliance]]-friendly faction located in the [[Tirisfal Uplands]] of the [[Tirisfal Glades]]. The survivors of the Army of Lordaeron are led by [[Captain Silas]] and base out of the [[Remnants Camp]], a derelict former outpost of the Army of Lordaeron.<ref name="Gheor">[https://discord.com/channels/466622455805378571/528228771594240030/1090029823910477845 Gheor from the Turtle WoW Community Discord] (dead link) - "The Tirisfal Uplands humans are what's left of his army."</ref> In addition to their main camp, they also hold the [[Shatteridge Tower]] and the [[Garrick Stead]].

==History==
===Background===
During the Third War, [[Dalaran]] was destroyed by [[Archimonde]],<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/The_Destruction_of_Dalaran_(WC3_Undead) The Destruction of Dalaran (WC3 Undead)]</ref> but many of the Burning Legion demons went to Kalimdor and were defeated.<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Twilight_of_the_Gods_(WC3_NightElf) Twilight of the Gods (WC3 NightElf)]</ref> By the time of the Third War, [[Othmar Garithos]] had risen to the rank of Grand Marshal. As the highest-ranking survivor of Lordaeron's military after the Scourge's rampage across Lordaeron, he recruited what forces he could muster from both volunteers and conscripted civilians. In addition to his human army, Garithos' forces comprised forces sent as aid from neighboring non-human states such as Ironforge. The healthiest blood elves led by [[Kael'thas Sunstrider]], prince of the ruined [[Quel'Thalas (kingdom)|Quel'Thalas]], also joined his army. Garithos did not enjoy having to work with the blood elves<ref name="A Dark Covenant">[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/A_Dark_Covenant_(WC3_BloodElf) A Dark Covenant (WC3 BloodElf)]</ref> or [[Dwarf|dwarves]],<ref name="A New Power in Lordaeron" /> believing that the [[Alliance of Lordaeron|Alliance]] should never have accepted the elves in the first place.<ref name="A Dark Covenant" /> Lord Garithos marshaled the survivors of the Alliance of Lordaeron and managed to retake Dalaran.<ref name="Misconceptions" />

In order to survive, the Remnants and particularly the blood elves hid caches of gold, lumber and artifacts such as magical small buildings all over western Lordaeron.<ref name="Shards of the Alliance" /><ref name="Misconceptions" />

===Blood elves===
The Alliance Remnants were stationed throughout Silverpine Forest. Prince Kael'thas and his blood elves were located near the shores of the Great Sea, though they were attacked by the Scourge and would've perished were it not for the help of the night elves [[Tyrande Whisperwind]] and [[Maiev Shadowsong]].<ref name="Shards of the Alliance" /> They returned to Dalaran but were scolded by Garithos for their tardiness and ordered them to repair three observatories.<ref name="Misconceptions" /> After the repairs, Lord Garithos went to the front lines and left Kael'thas to await orders. The next day an emissary sent by Garithos ordered the withdrawal of the human and dwarven troops from Kael'thas' command and sent them to the front lines. Then the dreadlord [[Dalvengyr]] and an undead army launched an attack on Kael'thas' bases. When the blood elves were going to be defeated, Lady Vashj and her naga appeared and helped Kael'thas fend off the undead. The combined armies attacked the undead and managed to kill Dalvengyr, but later Garithos arrived and saw the naga. He condemned the blood elves for consorting with naga as an act of treason and imprisoned the blood elves; planning to execute them later.<ref name="A Dark Covenant" />

===Divided===
The Alliance Remnants were thus divided into two groups: the human and dwarves loyal to Garithos and Kael'thas' forces, and the blood elves who were imprisoned.

Imprisoned and sentenced to death, the blood elves were rescued by Vashj. Kael'thas fought his way throughout the dungeons of Dalaran against Garithos' Enforcers and his former friend Jailor [[Kassan]]. The blood elves planned to reopen the portal opened by [[Kel'Thuzad]] that brought Archimonde into Azeroth and redirect it to [[Outland]], where they would then meet [[Illidan Stormrage|Illidan]].<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/The_Dungeons_of_Dalaran_(WC3_BloodElf) The Dungeons of Dalaran (WC3 BloodElf)]</ref> However, they needed to keep Garithos' Elite Guard at bay while his men crossed the portal. Kael'thas, Vashj, and some engineers planned a defense and managed to hold off Garithos until everyone made it through the portal.<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/The_Crossing_(WC3_BloodElf) The Crossing (WC3 BloodElf)]</ref>

===Mind-controlled===
Sometime after the blood elves escaped, and [[Arthas Menethil|Arthas]] left to defend the [[Lich King]], Garithos and his forces were launching offensives into the Plaguelands, and soon after they were bewitched and mind-controlled by [[Detheroc]]. Along with Detheroc's undead the Alliance Remnants fought the forces of [[Sylvanas Windrunner]] and [[Varimathras]], but were eventually freed from Detheroc's enslavement.<ref name="Dreadlord's Fall" /> Sylvanas then proposed an alliance with Garithos, to which he was offended by such an offer as Sylvanas had been part of the undead army that drove the humans out of Lordaeron in the first place. However, running out of military options, he reluctantly agreed to her terms: Garithos' army will aid her in her assault on [[Balnazzar]] in exchange for control of Capital City. Garithos assembled his forces and met with Sylvanas outside of her forward base.<ref name="Dreadlord's Fall" />

===Betrayed===
The elves had left the Alliance Remnants and the Wildhammer dwarves were seemingly annihilated,<ref>The Wildhammer are not in [https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/A_New_Power_in_Lordaeron_(WC3_Undead) A New Power in Lordaeron].</ref> with just humans and Bronzebeard dwarves left; yet the Alliance persisted and went to fight for the [[Capital City]].<ref name="A New Power in Lordaeron" />

Sylvanas, Varimathras, and Garithos planned to attack the Capital City. They knew that Balnazzar could only be defeated through attrition, so Sylvanas decided that they would assault his army from two fronts. Garithos' men would attack from the rear, while Sylvanas' forces would attack from the front. During the battle, Garithos' was informed that his dwarven reinforcements were lost. Infuriated, he went out to search for them. When he found them, he insulted them for their incompetence and commanded them to help him in the battle. With both armies attacking from two fronts, Balnazzar's Forces, the Dreadlord Insurgents, and the Dreadlord Loyalists were all defeated.<ref name="A New Power in Lordaeron" />

Balnazzar was "killed" by his brother Varimathras. After this, Garithos ordered Sylvanas and her undead "wretched animals" to leave his city. Sylvanas, however, turned on Garithos and ordered Varimathras to kill him, which the dreadlord gladly did.<ref name="A New Power in Lordaeron" />

Following the death of Grand Marshal Garithos, the survivors of his army rallied under the command of [[Captain Silas]], nestling themselves in the [[Tirisfal Uplands]]<ref name="Gheor" /> where they continued battling the Forsaken and attempted to make contact with the kingdom of Stormwind.<ref name="ACtA1" /> However, the Remnants' request for food, supplies and soldiers was denied by [[General Marcus Jonathan]].<ref>{{questlong|Alliance|17|A Call to Aid (2)|A Call to Aid}}</ref>

